{"anchor": {"begin": [70, 0, 460.67], "end": [70, 0, 672.0], "env": "definition", "file": null, "head": null, "id": 25, "kind": "approximate", "label": null, "labels": [], "line": null, "number": "6.5", "source_sha256": "102f9a82449c88fdc59d50cf96343c6b503788f2856c49c12c51e2d0390007a0", "statement": "Definition 6.5 (Labelled wave coefficients). For γ ∈ Γ and m ∈ Z \\ { 0 } , a smooth amplitude a γ ,m on E + γ belongs to W α if its local formulas agree whenever lifts represent the same common-torus point, satisfy (6.20) on overlapping neighborhoods, and ∂ θ a γ ,m = 0, supp(a γ ,m | E γ ) ⊂ Ω γ . It extends smoothly by zero across the slow and transverse support boundaries and both shell edges. On E γ ∩ {X a < X < X b } , its bounds are ∀I ∈ N5 0 ∃C j,I , b j,I , d j,I : | ∂ I a γ ,m | ≤ C j,I ε αS b j,I ∗ √︁ ζ δ −d j,IP v , 0 ≤ v ≤ L s . (6.29) These are amplitude derivatives; P v is only a pointwise weight. The continuation beyond v = 0, L s has no envelope bound or temporal zero-extension condition. Cut-off fields and sums. An actual cut-off coefficient additionally has supp a cut γ ,m ⊂ Ωcut γ and smooth zero extension in v. No divisibility by η γ , χ g , ψ is assumed.", "title": "Labelled wave coefficients"}, "blockers": [], "class": "proved", "clauses": [], "correspondence": {"by": "Christian Garry (drafted with Claude Code; second review by ChatGPT, checked)", "confidence": "medium", "coverage": "partial", "note": "The bound (6.29) with weight √ζ·P, uniform over labels in UniformWaveClass, on an abstract strip domain with an arbitrary envelope P. Not part of these definitions: agreement of local formulas across lifts, (6.20), ∂θ a = 0, supp(a|E_γ) ⊂ Ω_γ and smooth zero extension.", "source": "confirmed"}, "decls": {"NavierStokes.LabelSumBounds.UniformClass": "467fb28acdabf2046f5c2fb9", "NavierStokes.LabelSumBounds.UniformClass.mk": "e9a183834cfc769bd6d7d8d9", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.MemClass": "62106ad6201dad16f8dea1c0", "NavierStokes.WeightedClasses.Mem